    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0966" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/627: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-02T18:00:00-04:00">May 2, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Department’s instruction No. 346 of April 16 and Legation’s telegram 62 of
                    April 19. Navy Department has arranged to retain Colonel Matthews in command of
                    the Guardia until American officers are withdrawn. Please so inform Nicaraguan
                    Government in reply to its note of April 1, 1932.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d876-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Express to Colonel Matthews the Department’s appreciation for his sacrifice and
                    cooperation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
